flowchart TB
  subgraph Entry[Entry decision]
    U[Enter User ID]
    H{User ID is Host1234?}
    J[Ask Room ID and Password]
    G[Optional Join as Ghost]
    U --> H
    H -->|Yes| HD[Host Command Center]
    H -->|No| J
    J --> G
    J --> PL[Player Lobby]
    G --> GV[Ghost View]
  end

  subgraph Laptop[Host laptop]
    HD --> CR[Create room and set rules]
    CR --> WR[Word pack JSON and category filters]
    WR --> RD[Ready check]
    RD --> SR[Start: assign impostors randomly]
    SR --> TG[Drag order and Next Turn]
    TG --> RV[Host Reveal]
    RV --> NX{Continue or Restart}
    NX -->|Continue| WR
    NX -->|Restart| CR
  end

  subgraph Phones[Player and Ghost phones]
    PL --> RY[Tap Ready]
    RY --> EV[Tap envelope to reveal or close role]
    EV --> HI[Submit one locked hint]
    HI --> HB[See live hint board and active turn]
    GV --> HB
    HB --> RS[See reveal results]
  end

  subgraph Server[Local game server on host laptop]
    EX[Express JavaScript server]
    SO[Socket.IO room channels]
    ST[In-memory live room state]
    DB[(SQLite: rooms, players, rounds, hints, used words)]
    JS[(Local JSON: default and custom word packs)]
    EX <--> SO
    SO <--> ST
    ST <--> DB
    EX <--> JS
  end

  HD <-->|Host events and snapshots| SO
  PL <-->|Player events and private role updates| SO
  GV <-->|Ghost events and spectator updates| SO

  classDef warm fill:#F9F0DF,stroke:#8B3C35,color:#2D1C1A,stroke-width:2px
  classDef accent fill:#D96C4A,stroke:#5D2924,color:#FFF9F0,stroke-width:2px
  classDef data fill:#E5C46A,stroke:#775C1C,color:#2D1C1A,stroke-width:2px
  class U,H,J,G,PL,GV,HD,CR,WR,RD,SR,TG,RV,NX,RY,EV,HI,HB,RS warm
  class EX,SO,ST accent
  class DB,JS data

